    "problemStatement": "You are given a permutation PPP of length NNN.\n\nAssume you can perform two types of operations:\n\n\n\nModify PiP_iPi​ (1≤i≤N)(1 \\le i \\le N)(1≤i≤N) to any number at a cost of AAA.\n\n\n\n\nSwap PiP_iPi​ and PjP_jPj​ (1≤i,j≤N(1 \\le i,j \\le N(1≤i,j≤N, i≠j)i \\neq j)i=j) at a cost of BBB.\n\n\n\nWe define f(P,A,B)f(P, A, B)f(P,A,B) as the minimum cost to make the permutation satisfy Pi=iP_i = iPi​=i for all iii.\n\nYour task is to calculate:\n\n∑1≤i,j≤Nf(P,i,j)\\sum_{1 \\leq i, j \\leq N} f(P, i, j)1≤i,j≤N∑​f(P,i,j)Since the answer may be large, you need to output it modulo 998 244 353998\\,244\\,353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains an integers NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers P1,P2,…,PNP_1,P_2,\\ldots,P_NP1​,P2​,…,PN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output ∑1≤i,j≤Nf(P,i,j)\\sum_{1 \\leq i, j \\leq N} f(P, i, j)∑1≤i,j≤N​f(P,i,j). Since the answer may be large, you need to output it modulo 998 244 353998\\,244\\,353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Pi≤N1 \\leq P_i \\leq N1≤Pi​≤N",
      "It is guaranteed that PPP is a permutation.",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
